# CODEOWNERS — governed-path review ownership (docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md §18)
#
# The @deutsch-mate/* teams below are role-based placeholders. They MUST be created
# in the GitHub organization (with maintained membership) before branch protection
# can enforce these rules; until then GitHub silently ignores unknown teams.
#
# Per CODING_STANDARDS §18: API, event, migration, dependency, AI release, billing,
# identity, privacy, and infrastructure changes require reviewers who own those
# risks. Authors cannot self-approve changes to governed areas — branch protection
# must require review from someone other than the last pusher, and CODEOWNERS
# review must be marked "required" on protected branches.
#
# Later rules override earlier ones for the same path; keep the most specific
# rules last.

# --- Default: architecture owns anything not claimed below -------------------
*                                   @deutsch-mate/architecture

# --- Client/API contracts (OpenAPI is the machine contract, ADR-008) ---------
docs/openapi.yaml                   @deutsch-mate/architecture
packages/contracts/                 @deutsch-mate/architecture

# --- Database schema and persistence (ADR-009) -------------------------------
migrations/                         @deutsch-mate/data
packages/database/                  @deutsch-mate/data

# --- Repository governance, CI/CD, and infrastructure (ADR-019) --------------
.github/                            @deutsch-mate/architecture @deutsch-mate/security
infra/                              @deutsch-mate/architecture @deutsch-mate/security

# --- AI workflows, prompts, and evaluations (ADR-014, ADR-015) ---------------
apps/ai-worker/                     @deutsch-mate/ai-quality @deutsch-mate/security
evals/                              @deutsch-mate/ai-quality @deutsch-mate/security

# --- Billing and entitlements (ADR-016) ---------------------------------------
apps/billing-worker/                @deutsch-mate/billing @deutsch-mate/security

# --- Versioned curriculum content ---------------------------------------------
content/                            @deutsch-mate/content

# --- Authority documents (AI_CONTEXT.md authority order) ----------------------
docs/architecture.md                @deutsch-mate/architecture
docs/MVP_SCOPE.md                   @deutsch-mate/architecture
docs/PRD.md                         @deutsch-mate/architecture
docs/Database.md                    @deutsch-mate/architecture @deutsch-mate/data
docs/API.md                         @deutsch-mate/architecture
docs/AI_AGENTS.md                   @deutsch-mate/architecture @deutsch-mate/ai-quality
docs/DECISIONS.md                   @deutsch-mate/architecture
docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md            @deutsch-mate/architecture

# --- Waivers require the approving owner role (CODING_STANDARDS §1) ----------
docs/waivers/                       @deutsch-mate/architecture @deutsch-mate/security
